Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 10:46:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] TypeScript checker-choked rung: the linter refuses the bypass

A module is visible to every file, so the compiler never refuses an import
of it, and a TypeScript module chokepoint could only ever stand at
reference-choked. The project's linter can refuse it. @posthog/coherence/lint
is an ESLint v9 API plugin, coherence, with one rule, coherence/chokepoint,
which oxlint loads through jsPlugins.

The rule reads the spec, so the chokepoint is declared once: every
*.spec.md under its root, outside the config's ignore, through Coherence's
own spec parser. It acts on a bullet whose protects: is a module path and
whose chokepoint: is a module path or Name in file.ts, and follows the
check's import rulings (d-7abd1ba8): an import, import-equals require,
typeof import() or import() of the protected module outside the
chokepoint's module is a bypass, and an export-from or export * of it is a
re-export wherever it stands. Files in a test folder are exempt. Specifiers
resolve relative to the file or through the paths of the nearest
tsconfig.json above it, since a monorepo maps one alias differently per
package; no type information. Nothing is dropped in silence: a spec it
cannot read, a bullet it cannot resolve, and a root without a readable
coherence.config.json are reported at line 1 of each file under the
component, never thrown.

TYPESCRIPT_LADDER gains checker-choked between visibility-choked and
reference-choked, earned through the existing Visibility.rung seam as
Python's import-linter credit is. The adapter asks the rule's own reader
(lint-guards.ts) whether it guards that protected module with that
chokepoint's module, then looks for an .oxlintrc.json or .oxlintrc.*.json
whose folder holds the module, which loads the plugin, sets the rule to
error in its top-level rules with its root at the project root, and is
shadowed by no nested .oxlintrc.json without the rule. The enforcer names
the config. In every other case the adapter grades as before, and the
refutation stays Coherence's own.

The rule's tests run the real linter, oxlint 1.86.0 pinned as a
devDependency: red on each import and re-export form, green once they are
removed. Three new invariants and the ladder's, refuted eleven times with
the break staged and witnessed; full suite 366 tests, 0 fail.

